<main className={"view"}> <nav className={"secbar"} aria-label={"Research services"}> <div className={"wrap secbar__in"}> <p className={"secbar__k"}><a href={"/services/research-services/"}>{"Research services"}</a></p> <ul className={"secbar__l"}> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-543"}>{"Evidence synthesis "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-544"}>{"Design & protocol "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-545"}>{"Data & statistics "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> </ul> <a className={"secbar__cta"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Scope the study "}<svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"} /></svg></a> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-543"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l sbdrop__l--2"} style={{ '--rows': "4" }}> <a href={"/services/research-services/systematic-review/"}>{"Systematic review"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/scoping-review/"}>{"Scoping review"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/rapid-review/"}>{"Rapid & targeted review"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/living-systematic-review/"}>{"Living systematic review"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/evidence-gap-map/"}>{"Evidence gap map"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/meta-analysis/"}>{"Meta-analysis"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/network-meta-analysis/"}>{"Network meta-analysis & ITC"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/umbrella-review/"}>{"Umbrella review"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/literature-review-and-gap/"}>{"Literature review & gap"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-544"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l"}> <a href={"/services/research-services/experimental-design/"}>{"Experimental design"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/statistical-analysis-plan/"}>{"Statistical analysis plan"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/grant-writing/"}>{"Grant writing"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-545"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l"}> <a href={"/services/research-services/biostatistics-and-statistical-programming-services/"}>{"Biostatistics & programming"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/redcap-database-build/"}>{"REDCap database build"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/data-management-plan/"}>{"Data management plan"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/cdisc-sdtm-adam/"}>{"CDISC SDTM & ADaM"}</a> </div> </div> </nav> <div className={"crumbar"}> <div className={"wrap"}> <p><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M3 10.2 12 3l9 7.2V20a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-5v-6H9v6H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1z"} /></svg><a href={"/"} data-nav={""}>{"Home"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/"}>{"Services"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/research-services/"}>{"Research services"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><em>{"Scientific and Academic Writing"}</em></p> <span className={"crumbar__tag"}>{"Research that survives peer review"}</span> </div> </div> <section className={"phero"}> <div className={"wrap phero__in"}> <div> <h1>{"Scientific and Academic Writing Services"}</h1> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"Manuscripts are commonly rejected for poor structure or unclear writing — but far more often they are rejected for something a language edit cannot touch. In the best-documented study of why reviewers reject papers, the four leading reasons were inappropriate statistics, overinterpretation of the results, the wrong instrument and too small a sample. “Text difficult to follow” came fifth. Pubrica writes and rebuilds academic manuscripts, literature reviews, systematic reviews, theses and dissertations across the life sciences, medicine, engineering, the social sciences and the humanities — working on the argument and the reporting first, and on the English alongside it rather than instead of it."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions"}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#sw-gate"}>{"Check your manuscript"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#fsm-sw"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-sw"}>{"See a sample"}</a> </div> </div> <figure className={"jmatch rv is-in"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <figcaption className={"jmatch__bar"}> <span><b>{"Why reviewers actually reject"}</b>{" · 1,053 comments, 151 manuscripts"}</span> <span>{"Green is the one editing fixes"}</span> </figcaption> <div className={"jmatch__body"}> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Inappropriate or incomplete statistics"}</b><span>{"11.2%"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--no"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Overinterpretation of the results"}</b><span>{"8.7%"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--no"} style={{ '--w': "78%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Inappropriate instrumentation"}</b><span>{"7.3%"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--no"} style={{ '--w': "65%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Sample too small or biased"}</b><span>{"5.6%"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--no"} style={{ '--w': "50%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Text difficult to follow"}</b><span>{"3.9%"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "35%" }} /></div> </div> </div> <div className={"jmatch__foot"}> <p className={"funnel"}><b>{"Scope"}</b> <i>{"→"}</i>{" ethics "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" reporting "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" statistics "}<i>{"→"}</i> <b>{"language"}</b></p> </div> </figure> </div> </section> <div className={"creds"}> <div className={"wrap creds__in"}> <span className={"creds__lab"}>{"Every manuscript"}</span> <ul className={"creds__list"}> <li>{"Checked against the journal’s scope first"}</li> <li>{"Mapped to a named reporting guideline"}</li> <li>{"Authorship to the ICMJE criteria"}</li> <li>{"AI use declared in the publisher’s own form"}</li> <li>{"Read by a second person"}</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div className={"proof"}><div className={"wrap proof__in"}> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"From $450"}</b><span>{"Substantive scientific edit, up to 6,000 words, 7 business days"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"Since 2009"}</b><span>{"Academic and scientific writing for researchers and institutions"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"CONSORT 2025 · SPIRIT 2025"}</b><span>{"With PRISMA 2020, STROBE, ARRIVE 2.0, CARE, TRIPOD+AI and CHEERS 2022"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"ISO 9001:2015"}</b><span>{"Quality management certified · cert. H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N"}</span></div> </div></div> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our scientific and academic writing services"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Nine bodies of work, and each can be commissioned on its own."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Most authors need one or two. Buying the one you need is cheaper than buying a package built around it, and considerably cheaper than buying an edit when the problem is the argument."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--get rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Manuscript writing, from data to draft"}</b> <span>{"Written with you from your results, your outputs and your reading, not from a brief. The introduction narrows to one question, the methods are written so the study could be repeated, the results report what was found including what was not, and the discussion says what the data support rather than what the grant hoped — which is the second most common reason reviewers reject, at 8.7% of all comments."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Substantive and developmental editing"}</b> <span>{"Not proofreading. Structure, argument, the order the claims arrive in, whether the methods actually describe what was done, and whether every number in the text matches the number in the table. Language is corrected alongside, as a consequence of the work rather than as the whole of it. If proofreading is what you want, say so and it is cheaper."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Literature reviews, narrative and scoping"}</b> <span>{"Structured around a question rather than around what was found. Scoping reviews to PRISMA-ScR, with the caveat that PRISMA-ScR is currently under revision. Our fuller treatment sits on the "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"#/literature-review"} data-nav={""}>{"literature review and gap analysis"}</a>{" page, and the searches behind it on "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"#/literature-search-and-citation"} data-nav={""}>{"literature search and citation"}</a>{"."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Systematic reviews and meta-analyses"}</b> <span>{"To PRISMA 2020, with the protocol to PRISMA-P and registered on PROSPERO before the screening starts. A re-runnable search strategy with the database, interface, date and result count saved for every line, which is what makes the review updatable and what a methods reviewer asks for. Priced and explained in full on the "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"#/systematic-review"} data-nav={""}>{"systematic review"}</a>{" and "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"#/meta-analysis"} data-nav={""}>{"meta-analysis"}</a>{" pages."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Theses and dissertations"}</b> <span>{"Master’s and doctoral, worked to "}<i>{"your institution’s"}</i>{" handbook rather than to a generic format — word limits, chapter structure, the declaration, the reference style and the similarity threshold are set by your department and differ between departments in the same university. We also help convert a completed thesis into the two or three papers it contains, which is a restructuring job rather than an extraction one."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Reporting-guideline mapping"}</b> <span>{"The completed checklist, mapped to page and line numbers rather than ticked — which is what an increasing number of journals now require at submission and screen against before review. Done properly it also finds the real reporting gaps, which is the point: a checklist item you cannot map to a line is an item the manuscript does not report."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Cover letters, responses and appeals"}</b> <span>{"The cover letter argues fit and significance to this journal, which is the gate that stops most manuscripts before anyone reads the science. Point-by-point responses to reviewers are handled on the "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"#/response-to-reviewers"} data-nav={""}>{"response to reviewers"}</a>{" page; appeals against a rejection are worth attempting only where a reviewer made a factual error, and we will tell you honestly which case you have."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Journal and formatting work"}</b> <span>{"Journal selection against scope, indexing and aims rather than against impact factor alone; reference styling in APA, MLA, Harvard, Chicago, Vancouver or a journal’s own house style; figures, tables and supplementary files to the journal’s specification. See "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"#/journal-selection"} data-nav={""}>{"journal selection"}</a>{" and "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"#/manuscript-formatting"} data-nav={""}>{"manuscript formatting"}</a>{"."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Institutional and departmental programmes"}</b> <span>{"For universities, research labs and hospital departments: a standing arrangement across a cohort or a department, writing workshops delivered to your own researchers, and editorial support inside your own process rather than ours. Usually cheaper per manuscript and considerably more useful, because the second cohort needs less help than the first."}</span> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Disciplines and document types"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What we write, and where."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Medicine and the life sciences are the largest part of this work and not the whole of it. Where a discipline is outside what we can staff properly, we say so rather than accepting the project."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Medical and health sciences"}</b><span>{"Clinical research, public health, nursing, epidemiology, health services and health policy."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Life sciences"}</b><span>{"Molecular and cell biology, genetics and genomics, microbiology, pharmacology, ecology."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Engineering and technology"}</b><span>{"Biomedical, materials, computing and data science, with reporting to the field’s own conventions."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Social and behavioural sciences"}</b><span>{"Psychology, education, sociology, and the qualitative work that COREQ and SRQR govern."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Business, management and economics"}</b><span>{"Including health economics and the economic evaluations CHEERS 2022 covers."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Humanities"}</b><span>{"Where the conventions are different and a science template actively hurts. Edited by people who work in them."}</span></div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", borderTop: "0", marginTop: "0" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"What we do not do, and who should"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"We do not write a thesis for somebody to submit as their own work, and we do not sit an assessment. Where a university’s regulations prohibit third-party assistance, those regulations bind you and we will not help you around them; where they permit editorial support within limits, we work inside those limits and put the acknowledgement in writing. We do not guarantee acceptance by any journal, we do not place papers, and we have no relationship with any editor that could affect a decision — anyone who implies otherwise is describing misconduct. We do not sell authorship, and we will not add, remove or reorder an author at anyone’s request; authorship is decided by the four ICMJE criteria and by the authors. We are acknowledged for writing assistance, never listed as authors. And where your data will not support the paper you want, we will tell you that, decline to write the claim, and help you write the paper the data "}<i>{"will"}</i>{" support instead."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <nav className={"pagenav"} aria-label={"On this page"}><div className={"wrap pagenav__in"}><a href={"#pn-scientific-writing-who-we-serve-isfzec"} aria-current={"true"}>{"Who we serve"}</a><a href={"#pn-scientific-writing-our-compliance-wuu4j5"}>{"Our compliance"}</a><a href={"#pn-scientific-writing-how-it-works-1uo14mq"}>{"How it works"}</a><a href={"#pn-scientific-writing-our-experts-1r1j0mr"}>{"Our experts"}</a><a href={"#pn-scientific-writing-sample-work-1fkhbun"}>{"Sample work"}</a><a href={"#pn-scientific-writing-packages-dqbeg2"}>{"Packages"}</a><a href={"#pn-scientific-writing-guarantee-11l1qnn"}>{"Guarantee"}</a><a href={"#pn-scientific-writing-client-stories-1r0hmdi"}>{"Client stories"}</a><a href={"#pn-scientific-writing-faq-ol1q0x"}>{"FAQ"}</a></div></nav><section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-scientific-writing-who-we-serve-isfzec"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Who we serve"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Who commissions academic writing."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Six kinds of author, and one shared constraint: the work is finished and the paper is not, and the deadline belongs to somebody else."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"auds rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}><b>{"Doctoral candidates and research scholars"}</b><span>{"Thesis chapters, the papers a thesis becomes, and the first submission — usually with a supervisor who has read it too many times to see it. The smallest budgets and the most avoidable problems, which is why the readiness check exists at the price it does."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}><b>{"Faculty and principal investigators"}</b><span>{"Where the science is sound, the writing is competent and the constraint is time. Often three papers from one project, where the second and third are faster because the first produced a claim table and a search strategy worth reusing."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}><b>{"Clinicians who publish alongside a caseload"}</b><span>{"Case reports to CARE, observational work to STROBE, and audits that deserve to be papers. The scarcest resource is uninterrupted hours, and the commonest failure is a manuscript that was right in August and stale by December."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}><b>{"Researchers writing in an additional language"}</b><span>{"The disadvantage is documented: 38.1% report a language-related rejection against 14.4% of native speakers, and 42.5% are routinely asked to improve their English during revision against 3.4%. Real, worth addressing, and about a third of the problem rather than all of it."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}><b>{"Universities, departments and research labs"}</b><span>{"Standing arrangements across a cohort, editorial support inside an existing process, and workshops that leave your own researchers needing us less. The second cohort always costs less than the first, which is the point."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}><b>{"Independent researchers and think tanks"}</b><span>{"Outside a university’s editorial support and outside its subscriptions. Usually the strongest arguments and the weakest access to the literature that would evidence them."}</span></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-scientific-writing-our-compliance-wuu4j5"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our compliance and reporting standards"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Six frameworks, with the versions current on 21 September 2026."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Two of the big trial guidelines were replaced in April 2025 and the ICMJE Recommendations were updated this January. A supplier still writing to CONSORT 2010 is writing to a document whose own successor says it should no longer be used."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"stds stds--3"}> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"CONSORT and SPIRIT 2025"}>{"CONSORT"}<em>{"SPIRIT · 2025"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"CONSORT 2025 and SPIRIT 2025 "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(trial reports and trial protocols)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}><b>{"CONSORT 2025"}</b>{" was published in April 2025 simultaneously in the "}<i>{"BMJ"}</i>{", "}<i>{"JAMA"}</i>{", "}<i>{"The Lancet"}</i>{", "}<i>{"Nature Medicine"}</i>{" and "}<i>{"PLOS Medicine"}</i>{": thirty items and a flow diagram, with seven items added, three revised and one deleted. It states that CONSORT 2010 “should no longer be used”. "}<b>{"SPIRIT 2025"}</b>{" followed on 28 April 2025 with a 34-item checklist for protocols, and is blunter still — SPIRIT 2013 should no longer be used "}<i>{"or cited"}</i>{". One live caveat we do not skip over: the extensions, including CONSORT-AI, have "}<b>{"not"}</b>{" yet been realigned to the 2025 parent, and the 2025 statement tells you to keep using the existing extension in the meantime."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"PRISMA 2020"}>{"PRISMA"}<em>{"2020"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"PRISMA 2020 "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(systematic reviews and meta-analyses)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Still current: there is no PRISMA 2025 or 2026, and anyone telling you otherwise has not checked. The detail reviewers notice is that PRISMA "}<i>{"2020"}</i>{" was "}<b>{"published in 2021"}</b>{", in "}<i>{"PLOS Medicine"}</i>{" and four other journals, so a reference list dating it to 2020 is wrong. "}<b>{"PRISMA-P (2015)"}</b>{" for protocols has not been superseded. PRISMA-S covers the search report; PRISMA-ScR for scoping reviews and PRISMA-IPD for individual participant data are both listed on the PRISMA site as under revision, which is worth knowing before you build a protocol on either."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Observational and other designs"}>{"EQUATOR"}<em>{"by design"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"The rest of the EQUATOR library "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(one guideline per design)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}><b>{"STROBE (2007)"}</b>{" for observational studies, still the current version — there is no 2025 revision, and the commonly quoted item count is not actually stated on the STROBE site, so we cite the statement rather than the number. "}<b>{"STARD 2015"}</b>{" for diagnostic accuracy. "}<b>{"TRIPOD+AI (2024)"}</b>{" for prediction models, covering regression and machine learning together, with the 2015 explanation paper still the working document until its successor appears. "}<b>{"ARRIVE 2.0"}</b>{" for animal research: twenty-one items, of which the "}<b>{"Essential 10"}</b>{" are the minimum any journal will look for. "}<b>{"CHEERS 2022"}</b>{" for economic evaluations. "}<b>{"COREQ (2007)"}</b>{" and "}<b>{"SRQR (2014)"}</b>{" for qualitative work. "}<b>{"CARE"}</b>{" for case reports."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"ICMJE Recommendations"}>{"ICMJE"}<em>{"Jan 2026"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"ICMJE Recommendations "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(updated January 2026)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The "}<b>{"four authorship criteria"}</b>{" are unchanged and all four must be met by every author. Two things in the January 2026 update matter here. A new "}<b>{"Section V"}</b>{" covers the use of artificial intelligence in publishing, split between authors, reviewers and editors. And a new "}<b>{"Section III.L.2"}</b>{" states that all authors should be able to review the data supporting the results, and that with sponsored research this access should be written into the research agreement. A practical warning: the PDF carries the January 2026 text, while icmje.org’s HTML pages still showed January 2024 when we checked, so cite the PDF. Note also what the ICMJE says about services like ours — “writing assistance, technical editing, language editing, and proofreading” do not confer authorship. We are acknowledged, never listed."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"COPE and CRediT"}>{"COPE"}<em>{"CRediT · Z39.104"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"COPE and CRediT "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(ethics, and who did what)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"COPE’s position on AI is categorical: an AI tool cannot be listed as an author, because it cannot take responsibility for the work, and its use must be disclosed in the methods with the tool named. On paper mills, COPE’s June 2026 statement describes the problem as a hydra and gives no prevalence figure — which is the honest position, because nobody has a defensible one. "}<b>{"CRediT is ANSI/NISO Z39.104-2022"}</b>{", approved 14 January 2022, with fourteen contributor roles; most major journals now collect it at submission. Recording contributions while the work is happening takes minutes; reconstructing them at submission is where authorship disputes start."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Publisher AI policies"}>{"AI"}<em>{"4 publishers, 4 rules"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Publisher AI policies "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(which are not the same policy)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The one thing all four agree on is that an AI system cannot be an author. After that they diverge on the two points that matter to you. "}<b>{"Elsevier"}</b>{" (June 2026) wants a separate declaration statement published with the article and exempts basic grammar and spelling checking. "}<b>{"Wiley"}</b>{" (July 2026) also exempts tools used solely for spelling and grammar. "}<b>{"Springer Nature"}</b>{" uses a green/amber/red model rather than a single rule, and does not mandate where the disclosure goes. "}<b>{"Taylor & Francis"}</b>{" is the strictest: full tool name, version number, how and why — and "}<b>{"no stated exemption"}</b>{" for spelling and grammar tools at all. Assuming a common standard is how a declaration ends up wrong."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Where AI is used, and where it is not"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The author is you. That is not a formality."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Journals do not prohibit AI assistance; they prohibit undisclosed AI assistance, and they do not accept a tool as an author. The line Pubrica works to is that everything which reaches your manuscript has been read and verified by a person who can defend it to a reviewer."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--3 rv rv-d1"} style={{ marginTop: "0" }}> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we use it for"}</b><span>{"Finding source material. Checking references against the papers they cite. Consistency of terms, figures and cross-references. Structural suggestions a writer then accepts or rejects."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we do not use it for"}</b><span>{"Generating claims the data does not support; drafting a discussion without the results in front of a human; inventing or reformatting references without verification; and anything submitted without the declaration the journal asks for."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What goes in your declaration"}</b><span>{"The tool, the stage it was used at, and the human oversight applied — because journals, funders and the ICMJE January 2026 update all now expect it, and an undeclared tool found later is treated as a research integrity matter rather than a style preference."}</span></div> <div className={"caps__note"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Why we publish no accuracy figure of our own"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"These tools are marketed with precision and recall figures, and the honest problem is who measured them. In June 2026 a Cochrane journal retracted a validation study of one widely sold tool because every author held equity in the product, and the conflict had not been caught in review."}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"So Pubrica quotes no self-generated accuracy number, because ours would carry exactly the same conflict. What we will do is tell you which tool was used on your project, at which stage, and show you what a human changed after it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-scientific-writing-how-it-works-1uo14mq"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"How the scientific and academic writing service works"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Six stages, and the first one is not about writing."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Because the gate that stops most manuscripts is scope, and the gate that stops most of the rest is the analysis. Both are decided before a sentence is worth improving."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"steps6"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage one"}</span> <h3>{"Read the work, and say honestly where it stands"}</h3> <p><b>{"Before anything is quoted."}</b>{" What the study found, what it can support, which journal it is aimed at and whether that journal publishes this kind of work. Where the answer is that the target is wrong, we say so first, because a manuscript sent to the wrong journal is rejected by an editor in a morning regardless of how it is written."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage two"}</span> <h3>{"Map the reporting guideline onto the structure"}</h3> <p><b>{"CONSORT 2025 for a trial, PRISMA 2020 for a review, STROBE for a cohort, ARRIVE 2.0 for animal work."}</b>{" Each item located in the manuscript, or recorded as missing. Done at this stage it shapes the draft; done at submission it exposes a reporting gap on the day you wanted to submit, which is the single most avoidable delay in this process."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage three"}</span> <h3>{"Agree what the data will actually support"}</h3> <p><b>{"Before the discussion is written."}</b>{" Overinterpretation is the second most frequent reason reviewers give for rejecting — 8.7% of all comments in Bordage’s analysis — and it is almost always introduced at the writing stage rather than the analysis stage. We write the claim the interval supports, and where that is weaker than you hoped, you hear it from us before you hear it from a reviewer."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage four"}</span> <h3>{"Draft or rebuild, by a writer inside your field"}</h3> <p><b>{"Matched to the discipline and the design, not just to availability."}</b>{" Somebody who has written in your area reads your results the way your reviewers will. Every figure in the text checked against the table it came from, every citation opened rather than matched, and every reference checked for retraction — which is a real risk now and a quiet one."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage five"}</span> <h3>{"Declarations, contributions and the cover letter"}</h3> <p><b>{"The part that gets written at midnight and should not be."}</b>{" Authorship against the four ICMJE criteria, contributions in CRediT, competing interests, funding, data availability, ethics and consent, and the AI declaration in the exact form your publisher asks for — which differs between Elsevier, Wiley, Springer Nature and Taylor & Francis. Then the cover letter, which argues fit rather than summarising the abstract."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage six"}</span> <h3>{"Second reader, then submission, then the reviewers"}</h3> <p><b>{"Read by somebody who did not write it, against the checklist and the journal’s instructions to authors."}</b>{" You submit — the submission is made by the author, from the author’s account, under the author’s name. When the decision comes back, the person who wrote the manuscript is the person who helps with the response, and the drafting decisions behind every claim are recorded rather than remembered."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap band band--split rv"}> <div> <h2>{"Send the manuscript. We will tell you which gate would stop it."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"Two business days, at no cost: whether the target journal is right, which reporting guideline governs your design and what it is missing, where the discussion claims more than the results support, and an honest view of whether an edit is what you need. Sometimes the answer is that the manuscript is fine and the journal is wrong, which costs you nothing to hear."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "28px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#/pricing"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"jcard"}> <div className={"jcard__bar"}>{"What you provide"}</div> <div className={"jcard__body"}> <div className={"jcard__grid"}> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The manuscript"}</b><span>{"Or the results, if there is no draft yet"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The target"}</b><span>{"One or two journals, if you have them in mind"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The outputs"}</b><span>{"Tables, figures and the statistical output behind them"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The approvals"}</b><span>{"Ethics reference, consent, registration number"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The history"}</b><span>{"Any previous decision letters and reviewer comments"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The rules"}</b><span>{"Your institution’s handbook, if this is a thesis"}</span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"}>{"The previous decision letter is the most useful item on that list and the one most often held back, usually out of embarrassment. It should not be: a rejection letter tells us what a real editor in this field thought about this work, which no amount of guideline reading substitutes for. If a previous submission went badly, that is the document we most want to see."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"The gates, in the order they actually bind"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Which gate would stop your manuscript?"}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A desk rejection is a decision made in minutes against a short list of things. Tell the checker what you are submitting, what design it reports and what is already in the file, and it names each gate in turn, gives the reporting guideline that governs your design with its current version, and shows what the published evidence says about how much each gate actually weighs. It also gives your publisher’s AI disclosure rule, because the four largest publishers do not have the same one."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"tgrid"} data-tls={""} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <div className={"tk rv"} id={"sw-gate"} data-tool={"dsk"} data-open={"1"}> <div className={"tk__h"}> <p className={"tk__n"}>{"01"}</p> <div> <h3 className={"tk__t"}><button type={"button"} aria-expanded={"true"} aria-controls={"sw-gate-body"}>{"Desk-rejection gate check"}</button></h3> <p className={"tk__s"}>{"Six gates, the reporting guideline for your design, and your publisher’s AI declaration rule."}</p> <span className={"tk__tag"}>{"Runs in your browser · nothing sent anywhere"}</span> </div> <span className={"tk__x"} aria-hidden={"true"} /> </div> <div className={"tk__body"} id={"sw-gate-body"}> <div className={"tfm"}> <div className={"tf tf--wide"}><span id={"lbl-sw-type"}>{"What are you submitting?"}</span><div className={"tseg"} data-seg={"type"} role={"group"} aria-labelledby={"lbl-sw-type"}><button type={"button"} data-v={"art"} aria-pressed={"true"}>{"Research article"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"rev"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Review article"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"case"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Case report"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"thesis"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Thesis or dissertation"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"abs"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Conference abstract"}</button></div></div> <div className={"tf tf--wide"}><span id={"lbl-sw-dsgn"}>{"What does it report?"}</span><div className={"tseg"} data-seg={"dsgn"} role={"group"} aria-labelledby={"lbl-sw-dsgn"}><button type={"button"} data-v={"rct"} aria-pressed={"true"}>{"A randomised trial"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"obs"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"An observational study"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"sr"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"A systematic review or meta-analysis"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"dx"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"A diagnostic accuracy study"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"pred"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"A prediction model"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"anim"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Animal research"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"qual"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Qualitative research"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"econ"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"An economic evaluation"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"none"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"None of these"}</button></div></div> <label className={"tf"}><span>{"Where are you?"}</span><select data-k={"stage"}><option value={"draft"} selected={true}>{"Still drafting"}</option><option value={"done"}>{"Complete, not yet submitted"}</option><option value={"desk"}>{"Rejected without review"}</option><option value={"rev"}>{"Rejected after review"}</option><option value={"maj"}>{"Major revision requested"}</option></select></label> <label className={"tf"}><span>{"Who publishes the target journal?"}</span><select data-k={"pub"}><option value={"oth"} selected={true}>{"Not sure, or another publisher"}</option><option value={"els"}>{"Elsevier"}</option><option value={"spr"}>{"Springer Nature"}</option><option value={"wil"}>{"Wiley"}</option><option value={"tnf"}>{"Taylor & Francis"}</option></select></label> <div className={"tchk tf--wide"}> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"eth"} checked={true} /><span>{"An ethics approval or consent statement is in the manuscript"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"reg"} /><span>{"The study, protocol or review is registered"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"rchk"} /><span>{"A reporting checklist is completed and mapped to the text"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"cred"} /><span>{"Author contributions are recorded"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"coi"} /><span>{"Competing interests are declared"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"das"} /><span>{"There is a data availability statement"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"ai"} /><span>{"An AI tool was used in drafting"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"eal"} /><span>{"English is an additional language for the author team"}</span></label> </div> </div> <div className={"tout"} data-out={""}><div className={"tout__hd"}><b>{"1 of 6 gates clear"}</b><span>{"Structure first, prose second"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--hd trow--txt"}><b>{"Gate"}</b><span>{"What it is, and what the evidence says about it"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--mid"}><b>{"Scope and fit"}</b><span>{"The first gate and the one nothing on the manuscript fixes. In the only published study of desk-rejection reasons we could find — Wu and colleagues in "}<i>{"Communications in Transportation Research"}</i>{", 2024 — "}<b>{"55% of desk rejections were attributed to topic and scope"}</b>{", and the same authors warn that decision letters often do not give the real reason. Read three recent issues of the target journal before writing the cover letter, not after the rejection."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--gap"}><b>{"Ethics, consent and registration"}</b><span><b>{"An unregistered trial is the hardest gate on this list."}</b>{" The ICMJE requires prospective registration in a public registry before the first participant is enrolled as a condition of consideration, and registration after the fact does not cure it. "}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--gap"}><b>{"Reporting completeness"}</b><span><b>{"CONSORT 2025."}</b>{" Published April 2025 in the "}<i>{"BMJ"}</i>{", "}<i>{"JAMA"}</i>{", "}<i>{"The Lancet"}</i>{", "}<i>{"Nature Medicine"}</i>{" and "}<i>{"PLOS Medicine"}</i>{". Thirty items and a flow diagram: seven new, three revised, one deleted. It says of its predecessor that CONSORT 2010 “should no longer be used”. The extensions — CONSORT-AI, CONSORT-Outcomes and the rest — have "}<b>{"not"}</b>{" yet been realigned, and the 2025 statement tells you to keep using the existing extension in the meantime. "}<b>{"No completed checklist."}</b>{" A great many journals now require one at submission and screen against it before review, so this is a gate rather than a nicety. Completing it late also tends to expose a genuine reporting gap at the worst possible moment."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--mid"}><b>{"Statistics and interpretation"}</b><span>{"The heaviest gate in the evidence, and the one least often addressed by an editing service. In Bordage’s content analysis of 1,053 reviewer comments on 151 manuscripts, the top four reasons for rejection were "}<b>{"inappropriate or incomplete statistics (11.2%)"}</b>{", "}<b>{"overinterpretation of results (8.7%)"}</b>{", "}<b>{"inappropriate instrumentation (7.3%)"}</b>{" and "}<b>{"a sample too small or biased (5.6%)"}</b>{". None of those is a writing problem, and none is fixed by a language edit. Two of them — overinterpretation and incomplete reporting of the analysis — are fixed at the writing stage, by stating what the data support rather than what the discussion wants."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--gap"}><b>{"Authorship, interests and data"}</b><span><b>{"Contributions not recorded."}</b>{" The ICMJE’s four authorship criteria must all be met by every author, and “writing assistance, technical editing, language editing, and proofreading” do not confer authorship on anyone — they are acknowledged. CRediT, which is ANSI/NISO Z39.104-2022 and has fourteen roles, is the taxonomy most journals now use. "}<b>{"Competing interests not declared."}</b>{" Including the ones that feel too small to mention, which are the ones that surface later. "}<b>{"No data availability statement."}</b>{" The January 2026 ICMJE update added a new section on authors’ access to data: all authors should be able to review the data supporting the results, and with sponsored research that access should be written into the research agreement. "}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--has"}><b>{"Language and presentation"}</b><span>{"Ranked fifth as a single reason in Bordage’s analysis (“text difficult to follow”, 3.9% of comments) and ninth of ten as a category (9%). Worth clearing, and not worth buying a service for on its own if the first five gates are not clear."}</span></div><div className={"tverd"}><p><b>{"Structure first, prose second."}</b>{" Drafting is the cheapest point at which to fix any of this. Map the reporting checklist onto the section structure before writing, decide what the data will support before writing the discussion, and the manuscript that results needs an edit rather than a rescue."}</p></div><p className={"tsub"}>{"Declaring AI use, which is not the same rule everywhere"}</p><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Your target journal"}</b><span>{"The four largest publishers differ materially on two points: whether spelling and grammar tools are exempt, and where the disclosure goes. Elsevier and Wiley exempt basic language tools; Taylor & Francis does not. Read the instructions to authors rather than assuming a common standard, because there is not one. What is universal across all of them: "}<b>{"an AI system cannot be an author"}</b>{", because it cannot take responsibility for the work."}</span></div><p className={"tmeth"}><b>{"Sources, and a correction."}</b>{" Rejection reasons: Bordage G, “Reasons reviewers reject and accept manuscripts”, "}<i>{"Academic Medicine"}</i>{" 2001;76(9):889–896 — a content analysis of 1,053 reviewer comments on 151 manuscripts. Desk-rejection reasons: Wu J et al., "}<i>{"Communications in Transportation Research"}</i>{" 2024;4:100129. Language: Amano T et al., “The manifold costs of being a non-native English speaker in science”, "}<i>{"PLOS Biology"}</i>{" 2023;21(7):e3002184. Guideline versions from equator-network.org and each guideline’s own site; authorship and AI provisions from the ICMJE Recommendations PDF dated January 2026 — note that icmje.org’s HTML pages still showed the January 2024 text when we checked, so cite the PDF. Publisher AI policies read on the publishers’ own sites. All checked 21 September 2026. "}<b>{"The correction:"}</b>{" editing is sold as a way to “eliminate rejections due to language, formatting and scientific presentation issues”. No service can eliminate a rejection, and the evidence above says language is not usually why papers are rejected. You will not find that claim here. "}<b>{"There is no reliable published figure for how many submissions are desk-rejected"}</b>{" — PLOS, the most transparent publisher on editorial metrics, publishes acceptance rates and decision times and does not publish a desk-rejection rate. The confident percentages circulating on this question trace back to unsourced content, not to data, so we do not quote one."}</p></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d1"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", marginTop: "26px" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Five things to check on any editing page, including this one"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"Here is a test worth applying to any supplier, including us: read the first paragraph of the page selling you English-language writing. “The common reasons many manuscripts are rejected is due to poor structure or unclear writing” fails subject-verb agreement and then mixes two constructions, in one sentence, on exactly that kind of page. Then look for the other four. An offer to “eliminate rejections due to language, formatting and scientific presentation issues”, when rejection is an editorial decision no supplier controls. A headline figure such as “1 Million Researchers” with nothing behind it. A turnaround of “less than 8 hours” printed directly above a package table whose fastest tier is five to seven days. And "}<b>{"$"}</b>{", "}<b>{"$$"}</b>{" and "}<b>{"$$$"}</b>{" under a heading that says “Packages & Pricing”, which is worse than no price column at all, because it tells a reader the page was never finished. Real prices are further down, and they are the same per-word rate as every other service on this site."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-scientific-writing-our-experts-1r1j0mr"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our experts"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The people who will actually do the work."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Not a pool you are allocated from. The same named team stays with your project from scoping to delivery, the handover says which of them did which stage, and your project coordinator introduces them by name before anything starts."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"revw"}> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"SME"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Subject expert"}</b><span>{"A subject matter expert assigned from your topic, not from a rota"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Decides what the work is allowed to claim. Matched to your topic rather than allocated from a rota, and the one who tells you plainly when the evidence will not carry the conclusion you were hoping for."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Question, scope, interpretation"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"ICMJE, COPE, PRISMA"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Field"}</span><b>{"Matched to your topic"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DD"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Divya"}</b><span>{"PhD in Life Science · second reviewer"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Reads independently of the first pass and reconciles, because most errors in this work are transcription errors rather than reasoning ones. Disagreements are logged and adjudicated, never quietly resolved."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Independent second read"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"RoB 2, ROBINS-I, QUADAS-3, JBI"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Adjudicated by"}</span><b>{"A third reviewer"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DA"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Antony"}</b><span>{"Information specialist"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Finds what the work is built on. Writes the search line by line for each platform and hands it over dated and reproducible, so a reviewer, an editor or an assessor can run it again."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Search and retrieval"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"PRISMA-S, PRESS"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Second-checked by"}</span><b>{"A second information specialist"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"MJ"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Mr. John"}</b><span>{"M.Sc. in Statistics · statistician"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Owns anything the numbers decide. Says before the analysis exists whether the data can answer the question, and hands over the code so the whole thing can be re-run without us."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Analysis and certainty"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"GRADE, SWiM, CONSORT"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Tools"}</span><b>{"R, Stata, SAS, RevMan"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-scientific-writing-sample-work-1fkhbun"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Sample work"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The readiness report, which is where the money is."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Anybody can improve a sentence. What decides whether a manuscript survives the editor’s first ten minutes is whether it fits the journal, whether it reports what the guideline requires, and whether the discussion claims more than the interval allows. Use the tabs, then open the full report below and read the whole thing."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"sample"}> <div className={"doc rv"}> <p className={"doc__k"}>{"Pre-submission readiness report"}</p> <h3 className={"doc__h"}>{"Randomised trial · desk-rejected once · 6 gates checked"}</h3> <p className={"doc__sub"}>{"Scope · reporting · claims · references · declarations"}</p> <div className={"doc__tabs"} role={"tablist"} aria-label={"Parts of the readiness report"}> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"sw-t1"} aria-controls={"sw-p1"} aria-selected={"true"} tabIndex={0}><i>{"1"}</i>{"Gates"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"sw-t2"} aria-controls={"sw-p2"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"2"}</i>{"Reporting"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"sw-t3"} aria-controls={"sw-p3"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"3"}</i>{"Claims"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"sw-t4"} aria-controls={"sw-p4"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"4"}</i>{"References"}</button> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"sw-p1"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"sw-t1"}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Gate one: the first journal does not publish trials of this size"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Six of the last forty research papers in that journal were randomised trials, and the smallest enrolled 640 participants. This one enrolled 118. That is almost certainly why it came back in nine days without review, and no revision to the manuscript would have changed it. Three alternative journals proposed, with the scope evidence for each."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Gate two: registered prospectively, ethics statement present"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Registered before the first participant was enrolled, which is the ICMJE condition and the one that cannot be fixed afterwards. The registration number was in the methods but not in the abstract, where CONSORT 2025 asks for it. Moved."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Gate three: no CONSORT checklist, and the manuscript was written to CONSORT 2010"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"The flow diagram followed the 2010 template. CONSORT 2025 replaced it in April 2025 and says the 2010 statement should no longer be used. Rebuilt to the 2025 statement, and the checklist completed against page and line numbers."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Gate four: the primary outcome is reported without its confidence interval"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"A point estimate and a p-value, in both the abstract and the results. The interval was in the statistical output the whole time. This is the finding that would most likely have caused a rejection at the second journal too."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Gate six: the English needed work, and it was not the problem"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Twenty-two sentences rewritten for clarity and forty-one smaller corrections. Worth doing. Not worth doing on its own, and not what the first editor rejected it for."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"4 findings that would stop submission"}</span><span>{"Only one of them about writing"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"sw-p2"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"sw-t2"} hidden={true}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Guideline applied"}</dt><dd>{"CONSORT 2025, published April 2025. Thirty items and a flow diagram. The manuscript had been written to CONSORT 2010, which its own successor says should no longer be used."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Items fully reported"}</dt><dd>{"21 of 30. Located in the text and recorded by page and line, so the journal’s screener can find each one."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Items partly reported"}</dt><dd>{"6. Mostly the harms reporting, which gave totals without denominators, and the blinding item, which said “double-blind” without saying who was blinded — the exact ambiguity CONSORT has asked authors to stop using since 2010."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Items not reported"}</dt><dd>{"3. Changes to the trial after it started, how the sample size was determined, and where the full protocol can be accessed. All three were answerable from documents the team already held."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Flow diagram"}</dt><dd>{"Rebuilt to the 2025 template. The numbers did not reconcile: 118 randomised, 112 analysed, and six exclusions that appeared nowhere. They were legitimate and are now stated with their reason."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Extension checked"}</dt><dd>{"None applicable here. Worth noting that the CONSORT extensions have not yet been realigned to the 2025 parent, and the 2025 statement tells you to keep using the existing extension until they are."}</dd></dl> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"sw-p3"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"sw-t3"} hidden={true}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"“The intervention significantly improved outcomes and should be adopted in routine practice.”"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Rewritten to: “The intervention reduced the primary outcome by 8.4 percentage points (95% CI 1.2 to 15.6). The interval is wide and the trial was not powered for subgroups, so these results support a larger confirmatory trial rather than a change in practice.” The first version is the single most common reason reviewers reject after the statistics themselves."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"A secondary outcome described as “confirming” the primary"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"It was consistent with it. Three secondary outcomes were measured, none was adjusted for multiplicity, and the discussion leaned on the one that agreed. Now reported as exploratory, with all three shown."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"“No significant difference” used to mean no difference"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"In a trial of 118 participants, an underpowered null is not evidence of equivalence. Reworded, with the interval given so a reader can see what the trial could and could not rule out."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"The limitations section was already honest"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Single centre, short follow-up, and a sample size set by feasibility rather than by power — all stated plainly before we arrived. Kept as written, and moved earlier so a reviewer meets it before forming the objection."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"3 claims narrowed to what the data support"}</span><span>{"1 section kept exactly as the authors wrote it"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"sw-p4"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"sw-t4"} hidden={true}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"References checked"}</dt><dd>{"47, each opened and read against the statement it supports rather than matched to the citation."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Do not support the statement"}</dt><dd>{"4. Three had been inherited from another paper’s reference list rather than read at first hand, which is how a misattribution propagates. One supported a narrower population than the sentence claimed."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Retracted"}</dt><dd>{"1. Retracted nineteen months before the draft, and still cited as current evidence in the introduction. Removed, and the claim re-evidenced from two other sources. Nothing in a reference manager warns you about this."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Predatory or non-indexed sources"}</dt><dd>{"2. Both from journals not indexed in any major database. Replaced. Citing them does not invalidate the work, but it tells a reviewer something about how the literature was searched."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Style"}</dt><dd>{"Restyled to the second journal’s house format, with DOIs added throughout and the seven references that were missing page ranges completed."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Verified and retained"}</dt><dd>{"40 of 47."}</dd></dl> </div> <p className={"doc__foot"}><span>{"Redacted extract · field, intervention and every figure changed"}</span><span>{"Readiness report, as delivered"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"One manuscript, six gates, read in the order an editor reads them. "}<b>{"Use the tabs to see each check."}</b></p> <p><b>{"The gates tab carries the finding that mattered."}</b>{" The first journal does not publish trials of this size. Nine days, no review, no explanation beyond “not a priority for us”. Every hour spent improving that manuscript’s English before resubmitting it elsewhere would have been an hour spent on the fifth-ranked problem while the first-ranked one went untouched."}</p> <p><b>{"The claims tab is the one authors argue with, and should."}</b>{" Narrowing “should be adopted in routine practice” to what an interval of 1.2 to 15.6 percentage points supports feels like losing something. It is the difference between a discussion a reviewer engages with and one they use as the reason to reject."}</p> </div> <div className={"factors"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Scope checked before anything else"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Against what the journal actually published, not its aims page."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Reporting guideline version confirmed"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"CONSORT 2010 was still in the file eighteen months after it was superseded."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Every claim measured against its interval"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Not against what the discussion wanted to say."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"References opened, not matched"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Which is what catches a retraction nineteen months old."}</span></span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}>{"Ask for the sample work and you get a readiness report built round a manuscript like yours — same design, same discipline, same reporting guideline."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "16px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"#fsm-sw"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-sw"}>{"Read the full readiness report"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/insights/sample-work/"}>{"Discover more"}</a> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"fsm rv rv-d2"} data-fsm={""}> <button type={"button"} className={"fsm__t"} data-fsm-t={""} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"fsm-sw"}> <span><b>{"Read the full readiness report"}</b><em>{"The whole deliverable, on this page — the six gates, the CONSORT mapping, the claims narrowed, the references checked and what is handed over"}</em></span> <i aria-hidden={"true"} /> </button> <div className={"fsm__p"} id={"fsm-sw"}> <div className={"fsm__doc"}> <p className={"fsm__k"}>{"Scientific and academic writing · sample readiness report"}</p> <h3 className={"fsm__hd"}>{"Pre-submission readiness report — randomised trial, desk-rejected once"}</h3> <p className={"fsm__sub"}>{"A real readiness report with the field, the intervention, the institution and every figure changed. The gates, the categories of finding and the reporting format are as delivered. Ask us and we will build one around a manuscript like yours."}</p> <h4><span>{"1"}</span>{"The manuscript, and why it came back"}</h4> <p>{"A 118-participant randomised trial, submitted to a large general journal and returned in nine days without external review. The authors’ reading was that the English had let them down; two of the four authors are early-career researchers writing in an additional language, and that is the conclusion the market encourages. It was not the reason."}</p> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Element"}</th><th>{"How it was handled"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"What was read"}</td><td>{"The manuscript, the tables and figures, the statistical output behind them, the registration record, the protocol, the ethics approval and the decision letter."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Reviewer"}</td><td>{"A writer inside the discipline, plus a second reader who did not work on the revision. An author re-reads what they meant; a second reader reads what is on the page."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Scope"}</td><td>{"Checked against the last forty research papers the target journal actually published, rather than against its aims and scope statement."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Reporting"}</td><td>{"Every item of the governing guideline located in the text by page and line, or recorded as missing."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Claims"}</td><td>{"Every claim in the abstract and discussion measured against the estimate and interval in the results."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"References"}</td><td>{"Each cited work opened and read against the statement it supports, and checked for retraction and for indexing."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Declarations"}</td><td>{"Authorship against the four ICMJE criteria, contributions in CRediT, competing interests, funding, data availability and the AI declaration in the target publisher’s required form."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"What this is not: peer review. We check that the manuscript reports what the guideline requires, that every claim is supported by the result it rests on, and that it is aimed at a journal that publishes this kind of work. Whether the science is right, and whether it is important enough for a given journal, belongs to the reviewers and the editor."}</p> <h4><span>{"2"}</span>{"The six gates, in the order an editor meets them"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Gate"}</th><th>{"Finding"}</th><th>{"Resolution"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td><b>{"1. Scope and fit"}</b></td><td><b>{"Fails."}</b>{" Of the last forty research papers in the target journal, six were randomised trials; the smallest enrolled 640 participants. This trial enrolled 118."}</td><td>{"Three alternative journals proposed, each with the evidence for the recommendation: how many comparable trials each published in the last two years, the smallest sample among them, the indexing, the median time to first decision where published, and the article-processing charge. The cover letter rewritten to argue fit to the new target rather than to summarise the abstract."}</td></tr> <tr><td><b>{"2. Ethics and registration"}</b></td><td><b>{"Passes."}</b>{" Registered prospectively; ethics approval and consent statements present and complete."}</td><td>{"The registration number was in the methods but not in the abstract, where CONSORT 2025 asks for it. Moved. This gate cannot be fixed after the fact, so passing it is worth saying out loud."}</td></tr> <tr><td><b>{"3. Reporting completeness"}</b></td><td><b>{"Fails."}</b>{" No completed checklist, and the manuscript was structured to CONSORT 2010."}</td><td>{"Rebuilt to CONSORT 2025, which replaced the 2010 statement in April 2025 and says it should no longer be used. Checklist completed and mapped to page and line. Nine items were incomplete or absent; all nine were answerable from documents the team already held."}</td></tr> <tr><td><b>{"4. Statistics and interpretation"}</b></td><td><b>{"Fails."}</b>{" The primary outcome was reported as a point estimate and a p-value, with no confidence interval, in both the abstract and the results."}</td><td>{"The interval was in the statistical output throughout. Added everywhere the estimate appears. Three secondary outcomes reported as exploratory, unadjusted for multiplicity, rather than as confirmation."}</td></tr> <tr><td><b>{"5. Authorship, interests and data"}</b></td><td><b>{"Partly."}</b>{" Competing interests and funding present; no CRediT statement, and no data availability statement."}</td><td>{"Contributions recorded in CRediT — ANSI/NISO Z39.104-2022, fourteen roles — after a conversation with the authors, which also resolved a disagreement about the order of the middle two. Data availability statement drafted against what the ethics approval actually permits, which is narrower than the authors first proposed."}</td></tr> <tr><td><b>{"6. Language and presentation"}</b></td><td><b>{"Real, and fifth in line."}</b>{" Twenty-two sentences difficult to follow; forty-one smaller corrections."}</td><td>{"All corrected. Stated honestly in the report as the smallest of the five findings, because the alternative is to let an author believe their English is why a large journal declined a 118-participant trial."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"On the evidence behind that ordering: Bordage’s content analysis of 1,053 reviewer comments on 151 manuscripts ("}<i>{"Academic Medicine"}</i>{" 2001) found inappropriate or incomplete statistics the leading reason at 11.2% of comments, overinterpretation second at 8.7%, and “text difficult to follow” fifth at 3.9%. Writing and presentation as a category ranked ninth of ten. Wu and colleagues, looking specifically at desk rejections ("}<i>{"Communications in Transportation Research"}</i>{" 2024), found 55% attributed to topic and scope."}</p> <h4><span>{"3"}</span>{"The CONSORT 2025 mapping, item by item where it failed"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Item"}</th><th>{"As submitted"}</th><th>{"As revised"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Trial registration in the abstract"}</td><td>{"Absent from the abstract; present in the methods."}</td><td>{"Registry and number added to the abstract."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Sample size determination"}</td><td>{"Not reported."}</td><td>{"Stated as determined by feasibility within the recruitment window rather than by a power calculation, with the implications for precision carried into the discussion. That is a weakness and it is better stated than discovered."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Blinding"}</td><td>{"“Double-blind”."}</td><td>{"Who was blinded, stated individually: participants, the clinicians delivering the intervention, the outcome assessors and the statistician. CONSORT has asked authors to stop writing “double-blind” unqualified since 2010 because it means different things to different readers."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Changes to the trial after it began"}</td><td>{"Not reported. Two had occurred."}</td><td>{"Both stated with dates and reasons, and reconciled against the registry record, which had been updated for one and not the other. The registry was corrected."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Harms"}</td><td>{"Totals by arm, without denominators."}</td><td>{"Numerators and denominators for each arm, all adverse events reported rather than only those above a frequency threshold, and the serious events described individually."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Access to the full protocol"}</td><td>{"Not stated."}</td><td>{"Protocol deposited and the link given. Free to do, and an item a screener checks in seconds."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Participant flow"}</td><td>{"Diagram to the 2010 template; 118 randomised and 112 analysed, with six exclusions unexplained."}</td><td>{"Rebuilt to the 2025 template. The six exclusions were legitimate — four withdrawals and two protocol deviations — and are stated with their reasons and their timing."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"4"}</span>{"Claims narrowed to what the results support"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"As written"}</th><th>{"As revised"}</th><th>{"Why"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"“The intervention significantly improved outcomes and should be adopted in routine practice.”"}</td><td>{"“The intervention reduced the primary outcome by 8.4 percentage points (95% CI 1.2 to 15.6). The interval is wide and the trial was not powered for subgroup analysis, so these results support a larger confirmatory trial rather than a change in practice.”"}</td><td>{"A lower bound of 1.2 percentage points does not support a practice recommendation. This is the claim most likely to have drawn a rejection from a reviewer who read past the abstract."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"“This finding was confirmed by the secondary outcome.”"}</td><td>{"“A secondary outcome was consistent in direction. Three secondary outcomes were measured and no adjustment was made for multiplicity, so these are reported as exploratory.”"}</td><td>{"Selecting the agreeing outcome and calling it confirmation is the mechanism behind a large share of findings that later fail to replicate."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"“There was no significant difference in the subgroup, indicating the intervention is equally effective across groups.”"}</td><td>{"“The subgroup estimate was 3.1 percentage points (95% CI −9.8 to 16.0). The trial was not powered for this comparison and the interval is compatible with both benefit and harm.”"}</td><td>{"An underpowered null is not evidence of equivalence, and in a trial of this size it is barely evidence of anything."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"“To our knowledge this is the first study to examine this question.”"}</td><td>{"Removed."}</td><td>{"Two earlier studies were found in the reference check. Priority claims are trivially checkable and a reviewer who finds one wrong reads the rest of the paper differently."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The limitations paragraph, as written by the authors."}</td><td>{"Kept, and moved earlier in the discussion."}</td><td>{"It was already honest — single centre, short follow-up, feasibility-driven sample. A reviewer who meets a limitation before forming the objection reads a candid paper; one who meets it afterwards reads a defensive one."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"5"}</span>{"References, and the one nobody catches"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Check"}</th><th>{"Result"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Opened and read against the statement"}</td><td>{"47 references. "}<b>{"4"}</b>{" do not support the statement they are attached to — three inherited from another paper’s reference list rather than read at first hand, one supporting a narrower population than the sentence claimed."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Retraction and expression of concern"}</td><td><b>{"1 retracted"}</b>{", nineteen months before the draft was written, and cited in the introduction as current evidence. Removed and the claim re-evidenced from two other sources. No reference manager warns you about this; it has to be checked deliberately."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Indexing"}</td><td><b>{"2"}</b>{" from journals not indexed in any major database. Replaced with indexed equivalents. Citing them does not invalidate the work, but it signals how the literature was searched."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Completeness and style"}</td><td>{"Restyled to the new target journal’s house format. DOIs added throughout; seven references completed with missing page ranges."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Retained unchanged"}</td><td><b>{"40 of 47."}</b>{" Saying which references were fine is part of the report."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"6"}</span>{"Declarations, including the AI one"}</h4> <p>{"The authors had used a large language model to help draft two paragraphs of the introduction and to polish the abstract. They had not declared it, and were unsure whether they needed to."}</p> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Declaration"}</th><th>{"What was done"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Authorship"}</td><td>{"All four authors checked against the four ICMJE criteria, which must all be met. One contributor who had collected data but not met criteria two, three and four was moved to the acknowledgements, after a conversation with the corresponding author. That conversation is uncomfortable and it is far more uncomfortable after publication."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Contributions"}</td><td>{"CRediT statement drafted with the authors. Fourteen roles, assigned individually, which also settled a disagreement about the order of the middle two authors."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Writing assistance"}</td><td>{"Our involvement acknowledged in the acknowledgements, naming the company and what we did. The ICMJE is explicit that writing assistance, technical editing, language editing and proofreading do not confer authorship, and a supplier who offers to be invisible is offering you a problem."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"AI use"}</td><td>{"Declared in the form the target publisher requires, which is not the same across publishers. The four largest differ on whether basic grammar tools are exempt and on where the declaration goes. Here the model was used for substantive drafting rather than grammar, so it was declarable under every one of the four."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Competing interests, funding, data"}</td><td>{"Interests and funding were already complete. A data availability statement was drafted against what the ethics approval actually permits, which was narrower than the authors first proposed — an overpromised data statement is a problem you meet when somebody asks for the data."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"7"}</span>{"What was handed over"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Artefact"}</th><th>{"Why it matters afterwards"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"The revised manuscript, tracked"}</td><td>{"Every change visible, so the authors approve each one rather than receiving a new document."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The completed CONSORT 2025 checklist"}</td><td>{"Mapped to page and line, ready to upload. Several journals now screen against it before review."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The journal shortlist, with evidence"}</td><td>{"Three targets, each with what the journal actually published, the indexing, the decision times where published, and the charge. Reusable for the next paper from this trial."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The claim table"}</td><td>{"Every claim in the abstract and discussion, with the result it rests on. It is what makes the reviewer response tractable in three months."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The reference log"}</td><td>{"What was checked, what was replaced and why, including the retraction."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"The declarations pack"}</td><td>{"Authorship, CRediT, interests, funding, data availability, acknowledgement and the AI declaration, in the target publisher’s required form."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}><b>{"Outcome, stated the only way we are willing to state it:"}</b>{" the manuscript was submitted to the second journal on the shortlist and sent for review. We do not publish what happened next as though we caused it, because we did not — the trial did. What a readiness report changes is whether a manuscript is judged on its science or discarded for its paperwork, and that is worth buying on its own terms."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Benefits of working this way round"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What it changes, and what it cannot."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"No supplier makes a journal accept a paper. What a supplier can do is stop sound work being discarded for something that took an afternoon to fix."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"bens rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"01"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"The expensive gate is checked first"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"Scope, then ethics, then reporting, then the statistics, then the declarations, then the English. In that order, because that is the order an editor meets them and roughly the order the published evidence puts them in."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"02"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"You are told when editing is not the answer"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"If the manuscript is aimed at the wrong journal, or the discussion claims more than the interval allows, we say that before quoting for an edit. It costs us a sale roughly as often as you would expect."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"03"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"Reporting compliance worked, not assumed"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"The checklist your design requires, completed against page and line numbers, to the version current this month rather than the one in the template. CONSORT and SPIRIT both changed in April 2025."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"04"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"Language help sized honestly"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"If English is an additional language for your team, the disadvantage is real and measured: 38.1% of non-native speakers report a language-related rejection against 14.4% of native speakers. It is worth buying. It is about a third of the problem, not all of it, and we will not sell it as all of it."}</span></span></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-scientific-writing-packages-dqbeg2"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Packages"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Four tiers, with actual numbers in them."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A heading reading “Packages & Pricing” above a column of "}<b>{"$"}</b>{", "}<b>{"$$"}</b>{" and "}<b>{"$$$"}</b>{" is worse than publishing nothing, because it tells a reader the page was built and never finished. Here are the figures. Everything below is priced at the same per-word rate as every other service on this site, and every scope cap is printed beside its price rather than explained in an email afterwards."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"tiers tiers--4 rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Check"}</span> <h3>{"A readiness report, with no rewriting"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Authors who want to know what is wrong before deciding what to buy — and anyone holding a desk rejection they do not understand"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $190"}</b><span>{"up to 12,000 words · report only · no edit"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"3 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"All six gates, in the order an editor meets them"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Scope checked against what the journal actually published, not its aims page"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"The reporting guideline for your design, at its current version, mapped item by item"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Every claim in the abstract and discussion measured against its result"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"A journal shortlist with the evidence for each recommendation"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Credited in full against an edit or a rewrite commissioned within 60 days."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-sw"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-sw"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Check"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier tier--pick"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Edit"}</span> <h3>{"A substantive edit of what you wrote"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"A complete draft that needs structure, argument and language rather than a proofread"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $450"}</b><span>{"up to 6,000 words · $0.075/word above · 2 revision rounds"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"7 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Check, then the work itself"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Structure, argument and the order the claims arrive in"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Every number in the text checked against the table it came from"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Reporting checklist completed and mapped to page and line"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"References opened and read, and checked for retraction"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Declarations pack and cover letter drafted"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Proofreading alone — language and consistency, no structural work — is cheaper. Ask for it by name."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-sw"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-sw"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Edit"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Write"}</span> <h3>{"A manuscript written with you"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Results and outputs but no draft, or a draft that needs rebuilding rather than editing"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $1,200"}</b><span>{"up to 6,000 words · $0.20/word above · 3 revision rounds"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"15 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Edit, at manuscript scale"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Written from your data, your outputs and your reading — not from a brief"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Structure agreed against the reporting guideline before any prose"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"The claims agreed against the intervals before the discussion is written"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"A writer inside your discipline, who stays with it through review"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"The claim table handed over, which is what makes the reviewer response tractable"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"We are acknowledged for writing assistance, never listed as authors."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-sw"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-sw"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Write"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Long form"}</span> <h3>{"A thesis, or a department"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Master’s and doctoral candidates, and universities, labs and hospital departments buying for a cohort"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $2,400"}</b><span>{"up to 40,000 words edited · unlimited rounds in scope"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"20 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Worked to your institution’s handbook, not a generic thesis format"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Chapter-level structural work, not chapter-by-chapter proofreading"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Converting a finished thesis into the two or three papers inside it"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"For departments: a standing rate, and writing workshops for your own researchers"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Written confirmation of exactly what was done, for your declaration"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Where your regulations prohibit third-party help, we will not work around them. Send us the rules first."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-sw"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-sw"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Long form"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"psv rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"psv__i"}> <p className={"psv__k"}>{"What lands"}</p> <p className={"psv__n"}>{"The gate report"}</p> <p className={"psv__p"}><b>{"Six gates"}</b><span>{"each with its finding"}</span></p> <p className={"psv__t"}>{"In the order an editor meets them"}</p> <p className={"psv__d"}>{"Not a list of comments. Each gate either passes or does not, with the evidence for the verdict — including the gates that pass, because knowing your registration is sound is worth as much as knowing your discussion is not."}</p> </div> <div className={"psv__i"}> <p className={"psv__k"}>{"What lands"}</p> <p className={"psv__n"}>{"The completed checklist"}</p> <p className={"psv__p"}><b>{"Every item"}</b><span>{"mapped to page and line"}</span></p> <p className={"psv__t"}>{"CONSORT 2025, PRISMA 2020, STROBE — whichever governs"}</p> <p className={"psv__d"}>{"Ready to upload, in the form journals increasingly screen against before review. An item you cannot map to a line is an item the manuscript does not report, which is the point of doing it properly rather than ticking it."}</p> </div> <div className={"psv__i"}> <p className={"psv__k"}>{"What lands"}</p> <p className={"psv__n"}>{"The claim table"}</p> <p className={"psv__p"}><b>{"Each claim"}</b><span>{"with the result it rests on"}</span></p> <p className={"psv__t"}>{"And the ones narrowed, with why"}</p> <p className={"psv__d"}>{"Every statement in the abstract and discussion set beside the estimate and interval behind it. It is what stops overinterpretation getting back in during revision, and it is what makes answering a reviewer in three months a half-day rather than a week."}</p> </div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "22px" }}>{"Priced alongside any tier: proofreading alone, where language and consistency really are all you want; journal selection with the evidence for each recommendation; reference styling and reformatting for a resubmission; figure and table preparation; a point-by-point response to reviewers; statistical review by a statistician rather than a writer; plagiarism and AI-authorship screening; and expedited delivery where capacity allows, quoted on capacity rather than on urgency."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "24px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#/pricing"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-scientific-writing-guarantee-11l1qnn"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Guaranteed quality"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What we promise, and what we will not."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Editing is widely sold as a way to “eliminate rejections” and to improve “journal acceptance rates”. Acceptance belongs to the editor. Here are the terms as they actually are."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"gtee rv"}> <div className={"gtee__top"}> <p className={"gtee__k"}>{"The Pubrica guarantee"}</p> <h3 className={"gtee__h"}>{"We keep working until it is right."}</h3> <p className={"gtee__p"}>{"Revision until the manuscript meets the brief and the guideline it is written to, with no cap on rounds inside the scope agreed, and the writer available when the reviewers come back rather than reassigned to something else."}</p> </div> <div className={"gtee__grid"}> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"01"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Guideline versions checked twice"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"At the start of the project and again at delivery. CONSORT and SPIRIT were both replaced in April 2025 and the ICMJE Recommendations were updated in January 2026. A template carried forward is how that gets missed."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"02"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"The writer answers the reviewers"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"When the decision arrives four months later, the person who wrote the manuscript is the person who helps with the response, and every drafting decision is recorded rather than remembered."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"03"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"You get the working artefacts"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"The completed checklist, the claim table, the reference log and the journal shortlist — not just the manuscript. They are what make the next paper from the same project faster."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"04"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Our error, our cost"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"A guideline version wrong, a number mistranscribed from a table, a reference not checked — if it came from us, correcting it is free and you hear about it from us first."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"05"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Mutual NDA on request"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Signed before you send anything, in both directions, at no cost. Your question, your data and the fact that you are working with us stay confidential either way — and we will sign yours rather than insisting on ours."}</p></div> </div> <div className={"rate rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"rate__score"}> <b>{"9.4"}</b><span>{"/10"}</span> </div> <div className={"rate__body"}> <p className={"rate__t"}><span className={"rate__stars"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"★★★★★"}</span>{" Average client rating"}</p> <p className={"rate__d"}>{"From "}<b>{"3,000 responses"}</b>{" to Pubrica’s own post-delivery survey, sent to every client at handover, January 2024 to June 2026. It is our figure, from our records, and we say so rather than borrowing a badge."}</p> </div> </div> <p className={"gtee__foot"}><b>{"The limits, stated plainly."}</b>{" We do not guarantee acceptance by any journal, we do not influence editorial decisions, and we have no relationship with any editor or reviewer that could affect one — a supplier implying otherwise is describing misconduct, not a service. We cannot eliminate rejection and we will not claim to: the leading documented reasons reviewers reject are statistical and interpretive, and no editing service reaches them. We will not write a claim your data do not support, and where your discussion asserts more than your interval allows we will narrow it and show you why; if you want it left as written, it is your paper and your name, and we will say in writing that we advised against it. We do not write work for submission as somebody’s unaided own where an institution’s regulations prohibit assistance, and we will not help anyone around those regulations. We do not sell, add, remove or reorder authorship; authorship is decided by the four ICMJE criteria, by the authors. We are acknowledged for writing assistance and never listed as authors, and a supplier offering to be invisible is offering you a future problem. And we will not publish a testimonial claiming a publication outcome unless the client has confirmed it in writing and is willing to be named."}</p> </div> <div style={{ height: "clamp(26px,3vw,38px)" }} /> <div className={"pledges rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"The scope check is free"}</p> <p>{"Send an abstract and the journal you are aiming at, and we will tell you whether that journal publishes this kind of work — measured against what it actually printed in the last two years, not against its aims and scope page. Two business days, no cost, no obligation. It is the gate that stops most manuscripts, it is the one nothing in the manuscript fixes, and it takes us under an hour. Occasionally the answer is that your paper is fine and your target is wrong, which is the cheapest useful thing anyone will tell you all year."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Your unpublished work stays yours"}</p> <p>{"A non-disclosure agreement is signed before any material moves, and writers and project staff are bound by internal confidentiality agreements as well. Unpublished data, drafts and decision letters are held under the UK GDPR on access-controlled systems within a quality management system certified to ISO 9001:2015 — certificate H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N — kept only as long as the project needs them, never used to train anything, and never shared outside your project team. We do not reuse your text, your figures or your search strategies on anyone else’s project, and we do not publish your work as a sample; every sample on this site is redacted or composite, and the same undertaking covers yours."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Declared, not ghosted"}</p> <p>{"Our involvement goes in the acknowledgements, naming the company and what we did. The ICMJE is explicit that writing assistance, technical editing, language editing and proofreading do not confer authorship, and Springer Nature asks for the funding source of editorial help as well. Any use of AI in the work is declared to you and then declared in your manuscript in the exact form your publisher requires — which differs between Elsevier, Wiley, Springer Nature and Taylor & Francis, and assuming a common standard is how a declaration ends up wrong."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Working inside your rules, not ours"}</p> <p>{"Your institution’s handbook, your department’s chapter structure, your supervisor’s preferences, your journal’s house style. Where a university permits editorial support within defined limits, we work inside those limits and give you written confirmation of exactly what was done, so you can make the declaration your regulations ask for. Where it prohibits assistance, we decline the work. Send us the rules at the start and the conversation is short; send them at the end and it is not."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-scientific-writing-client-stories-1r0hmdi"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"In their words"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Three manuscripts, and what changed."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Rephrased from client feedback. Each quote is a placeholder until the named client has confirmed it in writing, which matters more on this page than most. A figure like “a million researchers already use our recommendations” is easy to print and impossible to evidence, so you will not find one here."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"tcar rv"}> <div className={"tcar__track"} data-tcar={""} tabIndex={0} role={"group"} aria-label={"Client testimonials, scrollable"}> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“They told me the journal was wrong before they quoted for the edit. I had assumed my English was the problem for two months.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}><span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--c"}><span className={"mcov__k"}>{"RANDOMISED"}<br />{"TRIAL"}</span><span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Readiness"}<br />{"Report"}</span><span className={"mcov__r"} /></span></span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Postdoctoral researcher · institution to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Delivered as"}</b><span>{"Readiness report and journal shortlist"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“One of our references had been retracted a year and a half earlier and we were still citing it as current evidence.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}><span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--b"}><span className={"mcov__k"}>{"SYSTEMATIC"}<br />{"REVIEW"}</span><span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Manuscript"}<br />{"Edit"}</span><span className={"mcov__r"} /></span></span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Senior lecturer · institution to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Delivered as"}</b><span>{"Substantive edit and reference log"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“They narrowed three claims in the discussion and showed me the intervals. I argued about two of them and they were right about both.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}><span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--e"}><span className={"mcov__k"}>{"COHORT"}<br />{"STUDY"}</span><span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Manuscript"}<br />{"Written"}</span><span className={"mcov__r"} /></span></span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Principal investigator · institution to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Delivered as"}</b><span>{"Manuscript, claim table and declarations pack"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> </div> <div className={"tcar__foot"}> <a className={"btn btn--ghost tcar__more"} href={"/testimonial/"}>{"Explore more client testimonials"}</a> <div className={"tcar__dots"} data-tdots={""} aria-hidden={"true"} style={{ display: "none" }} /> <div className={"tcar__btns"} style={{ display: "none" }}> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tprev={""} aria-label={"Previous testimonial"} disabled={true}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tnext={""} aria-label={"More testimonials"} disabled={true}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-scientific-writing-faq-ol1q0x"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"} style={{ display: "block" }}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Scientific and academic writing FAQs"}</p> <h2>{"Eleven questions researchers ask."}</h2> <p className={"prose"} style={{ marginTop: "20px" }}>{"Not sure whether you need an edit, a rewrite or a different journal? "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Ask an expert"}</a>{" — no quote required."}</p> </div> <div className={"faq__list rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sw-0"}><span>{"What kinds of academic documents do you write and edit?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"sw-0"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Research articles and short reports; narrative, scoping and systematic reviews; meta-analyses; case reports to CARE; theses and dissertations at master’s and doctoral level, and the papers that come out of them; conference abstracts and posters; book chapters; and the supporting documents that decide whether any of them are read — cover letters, responses to reviewers, data availability and declaration statements, and completed reporting checklists. Across medicine and the health sciences, the life sciences, engineering and computing, psychology and the social sciences, economics and management, and the humanities. Where a discipline is outside what we can staff properly, we say so and decline rather than assigning a writer who will learn your field on your manuscript."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sw-1"}><span>{"Will editing get my paper accepted?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"sw-1"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"No, and the honest version of the answer is more useful than the reassuring one. You will see editing offered as a way to “eliminate rejections due to language, formatting and scientific presentation issues”. In the best-documented study of why reviewers reject — Bordage’s content analysis of 1,053 comments on 151 manuscripts — the leading reasons were "}<b>{"inappropriate or incomplete statistics (11.2%)"}</b>{", "}<b>{"overinterpretation of the results (8.7%)"}</b>{", "}<b>{"inappropriate instrumentation (7.3%)"}</b>{" and "}<b>{"a sample too small or biased (5.6%)"}</b>{". “Text difficult to follow” came fifth at 3.9%, and writing and presentation as a category ranked ninth of ten. An edit reaches the fifth-ranked problem. What actually improves your odds is fixing the ones above it — which mostly means reporting what you did completely, and claiming only what the interval supports. Note also that no publisher-affiliated editing service claims otherwise: Elsevier’s own guarantee on its editing pages is a re-edit or a refund, not an outcome."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sw-2"}><span>{"What proportion of papers are desk-rejected?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"sw-2"} role={"region"}><div><p><b>{"Nobody knows, and any page giving you a confident percentage is repeating something unsourced."}</b>{" We looked for a publisher-wide figure and there is not one. PLOS, which publishes more editorial data than almost anyone, publishes acceptance rates and decision times by journal and does "}<i>{"not"}</i>{" publish a desk-rejection rate. What exists is scattered: a peer-reviewed study of 128,454 manuscripts across 25 Nature-branded journals found 34% desk-rejected under single-blind review and 45% under double-blind; "}<i>{"Nature"}</i>{" itself says only that about 8% of submissions are accepted and that most are declined without review. So the honest range is roughly a third to two-thirds depending on the journal’s selectivity, with no industry figure. We mention this because the top of the search results for this exact question is now largely synthetic content with confident numbers and no sources, and a supplier quoting one of those is telling you how it checks things."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sw-3"}><span>{"What is your turnaround?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"sw-3"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Readiness report "}<b>{"3 business days"}</b>{"; substantive edit "}<b>{"7"}</b>{"; a manuscript written with you "}<b>{"15"}</b>{"; a thesis or long-form project "}<b>{"20"}</b>{". Those are the bands, and they are what we will quote against. A turnaround of “less than 8 hours” advertised directly above a package table whose fastest tier is five to seven days cannot be true in both places. Read the table rather than the headline, here and anywhere else. Two things move a real timeline more than word count does: how complete the material is — a manuscript waiting on final analysis outputs is not a writing problem — and your own review cycles, which are almost always the long pole. A paper drafted in fifteen days and reviewed by five co-authors over seven weeks took nine weeks. Expedited delivery is available where capacity allows and is quoted on capacity rather than on urgency; where a date is not achievable we say so rather than taking the fee and missing it."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sw-4"}><span>{"Is using a writing service allowed? Do I have to declare it?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"sw-4"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"For journal articles: allowed, and yes, declare it. We found no journal or publisher that prohibits professional editing. Elsevier requires that anyone who participated in substantive aspects such as language editing or medical writing is recognised in the acknowledgements. Springer Nature and BMC require the same "}<b>{"and"}</b>{" the funding source of that assistance, and warn that unacknowledged editorial services may constitute an undisclosed conflict of interest. The ICMJE is explicit that writing assistance, technical editing, language editing and proofreading do not qualify anyone for authorship — they are acknowledged. So we are named in your acknowledgements, with what we did. "}<b>{"For a thesis or any assessed work, the rule is your institution’s, not ours"}</b>{", and institutions differ sharply: some permit language editing within defined limits, some require a declaration, some prohibit third-party assistance entirely. Send us the regulations before you send us the thesis. Where they permit help, we work inside the limits and give you written confirmation of exactly what was done so your declaration is accurate. Where they prohibit it, we decline."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sw-5"}><span>{"Do I have to declare AI use, and where?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"sw-5"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Almost certainly yes, and "}<b>{"the rule is not the same at every publisher"}</b>{", which is the part that catches people. All of them agree an AI system cannot be an author, because it cannot take responsibility for the work. After that: "}<b>{"Elsevier"}</b>{" (updated June 2026) wants a separate declaration statement in the manuscript at submission, published with the article, and exempts basic grammar and spelling checking. "}<b>{"Wiley"}</b>{" (July 2026) requires disclosure of every tool, its purpose, whether it influenced key arguments and how you verified the output — and also exempts tools used solely for spelling and grammar. "}<b>{"Springer Nature"}</b>{" uses a green/amber/red model rather than one rule, with accountability for content explicitly not delegable to an AI system, and does not mandate where the disclosure goes. "}<b>{"Taylor & Francis"}</b>{" is the strictest and the one with "}<b>{"no stated exemption"}</b>{" for grammar tools: full tool name, version number, how it was used and why. The ICMJE’s January 2026 update added a whole new section on AI in publishing. Check your target journal’s instructions to authors rather than assuming a common standard, because there is not one."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sw-6"}><span>{"Which reporting guideline applies to my study?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"sw-6"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"By design, at the versions current on 21 September 2026: randomised trials "}<b>{"CONSORT 2025"}</b>{" and their protocols "}<b>{"SPIRIT 2025"}</b>{" — both published in April 2025, and both stating that their 2013 and 2010 predecessors should no longer be used. Systematic reviews and meta-analyses "}<b>{"PRISMA 2020"}</b>{", which despite its name was published in 2021, with "}<b>{"PRISMA-P (2015)"}</b>{" for the protocol. Observational studies "}<b>{"STROBE (2007)"}</b>{", still current — there is no 2025 revision. Diagnostic accuracy "}<b>{"STARD 2015"}</b>{". Prediction models "}<b>{"TRIPOD+AI (2024)"}</b>{", with the 2015 explanation paper still the working document until its successor appears. Animal research "}<b>{"ARRIVE 2.0"}</b>{", whose Essential 10 items are the minimum any journal looks for. Economic evaluations "}<b>{"CHEERS 2022"}</b>{". Qualitative work "}<b>{"COREQ (2007)"}</b>{" or "}<b>{"SRQR (2014)"}</b>{", depending on the journal. Case reports "}<b>{"CARE"}</b>{". One caveat we do not skip: the CONSORT extensions, including CONSORT-AI, have not yet been realigned to the 2025 parent, and the 2025 statement tells you to keep using the existing extension in the meantime. If your design is not on that list, the EQUATOR Network indexes several hundred more and we will search it for you."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sw-7"}><span>{"English is not my first language. How much does that actually cost me?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"sw-7"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"It is measurable, and it is smaller than the market selling you editing implies. Amano and colleagues surveyed 908 environmental scientists across eight nationalities ("}<i>{"PLOS Biology"}</i>{", 2023). "}<b>{"38.1%"}</b>{" of researchers from moderate-proficiency countries and "}<b>{"35.9%"}</b>{" from low-proficiency countries reported having had a paper rejected because of English writing, against "}<b>{"14.4%"}</b>{" of native speakers — a rate 2.5 to 2.6 times higher. The revision burden is the starker number: "}<b>{"42.5%"}</b>{" of non-native speakers are often or always asked to improve their English during revision, against "}<b>{"3.4%"}</b>{" of native speakers. Reading a paper took early-career non-native speakers up to 91% longer; around 30% often or always decline to attend English-language conferences because of it. Three things follow. The disadvantage is real and language editing is worth buying if this is you. It accounts for roughly a third of non-native-speaker rejections, not all of them — and native speakers are rejected for language too. And one detail we will not smooth over: in that study the moderate-proficiency group reported a "}<i>{"larger"}</i>{" time penalty than the low-proficiency group for writing and presentations, which is what the paper says and not what a neat story would want it to say."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sw-8"}><span>{"Who owns the work, and is my unpublished data safe?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"sw-8"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"You own it — the manuscript, the data, the figures and every artefact we hand over. A non-disclosure agreement is signed before any material moves, and writers and project staff are bound by internal confidentiality agreements as well. Unpublished data, drafts and decision letters are held under the UK GDPR on access-controlled systems within a quality management system certified to ISO 9001:2015, certificate H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N, kept only as long as the project needs them and never used to train anything. We do not reuse your text, figures or search strategies on anyone else’s project, and we do not publish your work as a sample: every sample on this site is redacted or composite. Pubrica will never send you somebody else’s actual manuscript, because the same undertaking covers yours."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sw-9"}><span>{"Can I see a sample before ordering?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"sw-9"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Yes, and there is a complete one on this page — a pre-submission readiness report for a randomised trial that had been desk-rejected once, with the field, the intervention, the institution and every figure changed. Open it above and read the whole thing without asking us for anything, including the parts where the finding was that the authors were right and we changed nothing. If you want something closer to your own work, ask and we will build one round a manuscript like yours: same design, same discipline, same reporting guideline. Two honest caveats. Client work is confidential, so any sample is redacted or composite. And a sample shows method, citation discipline and how findings are reported back to you; it cannot show whether the writer understood "}<i>{"your"}</i>{" study, which is what the free scope check is for."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sw-10"}><span>{"What happens if I am not satisfied?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"sw-10"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"We revise until the manuscript meets the brief and the guideline it is written to, with no cap on rounds inside the scope agreed. Two things keep that workable rather than open-ended. The structure is agreed against the reporting guideline before any prose is written, so a revision is a revision rather than a restart — most dissatisfaction with a manuscript traces back to a structure nobody signed off. And scope is written down: a new analysis, a different journal’s complete reformatting, or a second paper from the same data is new work, and we say which side of that line something falls on before starting rather than after. Where the problem is ours — a guideline version wrong, a number mistranscribed from a table, a reference not opened — correcting it is free and you hear about it from us first. One thing we will not do on request: put back a claim we narrowed. If you want it as you wrote it, it is your paper and your name, and we will restore it and record in writing that we advised against it."}</p></div></div></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Related services"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What sits either side of a manuscript."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"The evidence underneath it, the numbers inside it, and what happens after you press submit."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"rel"}> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"1"}</span><b>{"BEFORE THE DRAFT"}</b><em>{"evidence and design"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/literature-review-and-gap/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Literature review and gap analysis"}</b><span>{"Structured round a question, with gaps named specifically enough to verify."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/biostatistics-and-statistical-programming-services/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Biostatistics and programming"}</b><span>{"The analysis behind the paper, with reproducible code and outputs."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"2"}</span><b>{"ALONGSIDE IT"}</b><em>{"checking and preparing"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/publication-support/peer-review-pre-submission/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Pre-submission peer review"}</b><span>{"The objection arrives from us first, where it costs a week rather than a cycle."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/publication-support/journal-selection/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Journal selection"}</b><span>{"Against scope and indexing, with the evidence for every recommendation."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"3"}</span><b>{"AFTER SUBMISSION"}</b><em>{"review and revision"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/publication-support/responding-to-reviewers/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Response to reviewer comments"}</b><span>{"Point by point, with the disagreements argued rather than conceded."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/medical-writing/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Medical writing"}</b><span>{"The clinical and regulatory side of the same discipline."}</span></a> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Insights"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Further reading on getting published."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Three pieces on the funder mandates that now decide where a paper can go and who pays for it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"reads rv rv-d1"}> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/nih-public-access-policy-2025/"} data-nav={""}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"NIH Public Access Policy 2025: what changed"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"The twelve-month embargo is gone. What that means for where NIH-funded work can be submitted, and when."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/horizon-europe-article-processing-charges/"} data-nav={""}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"Horizon Europe will not pay a hybrid journal APC"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"A funding rule that quietly removes a large number of journals from the shortlist before scope is even considered."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/japan-immediate-open-access/"} data-nav={""}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"Japan’s immediate open access rule from FY2025"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"What the requirement covers, which outputs it reaches, and how it changes journal selection for funded researchers."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight section--dark"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap cta cta__in"}> <div className={"rv"}> <h2>{"Send an abstract and a journal. The scope check is free."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"We will tell you whether that journal publishes work like yours — measured against what it actually printed, not against its aims page. Two business days, no cost, no obligation. It is the gate that stops most manuscripts and the one nothing in the manuscript fixes."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d1"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Contact us"}</a> </div> </div> </section> </main>
